From 5fb10c7737631aea5354f2e228184fb877c3f869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HR_Z <2463882771@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:20:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Suppress progress-code output entirely

The handler gated progress codes on the INFO level, which put them in direct conflict
with the diagnostics we need: VerifiedBootDxe reports at INFO, so enabling INFO also
brought back one start and one end line per driver - roughly 280 lines, several
kilobytes of a 64 KB log ring, for information the dispatcher already conveys by
naming the driver before it runs. A hang still shows as the last driver named.

Dropped outright rather than re-gated, so INFO can stay on for the drivers that need
it.
---
 .../Serial/Common/SerialStatusCodeHandler.c   | 328 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 166 insertions(+), 162 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MsCorePkg/Universal/StatusCodeHandler/Serial/Common/SerialStatusCodeHandler.c b/MsCorePkg/Universal/StatusCodeHandler/Serial/Common/SerialStatusCodeHandler.c
index 6fd5c52..11274a5 100644
--- a/MsCorePkg/Universal/StatusCodeHandler/Serial/Common/SerialStatusCodeHandler.c
+++ b/MsCorePkg/Universal/StatusCodeHandler/Serial/Common/SerialStatusCodeHandler.c
@@ -1,162 +1,166 @@
